#~ msgid ""
#~ "Other than declared arrays in lists there is no way to jump to determine the address of the nth element other than iterating from one element to the other until the nth element is reached. Which isn't a maxima-specific phenomenon but the price one has to pay for lists being way easier to resize than declared arrays. If the address of the current element is known iterating to the next one is trivial, though, so\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "   for i in list do <something>\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "or\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "   makelist(expression,i,list)\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "provide highly efficient ways to do something on every list element."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "除了声明为数组之外，要确定列表中第 n 个元素的地址，只能从一个元素迭代到另一个元素，直至到达第 n 个元素，而没有其他方法可以直接跳转。这并不是 Maxima 特有的现象，而是列表拥有比数组更容易调整大小的优点而付出的代价。如果当前元素的地址是已知的，那么迭代到下一个元素是简单的，例如\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "   for i in list do <something>\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "或者\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "   makelist(expression,i,list)\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ "为对每个列表元素操作提供了高效的方法。"

